# Environment variables read by the engine (ambient env only — the engine does
# NOT load .env files itself; export these in your shell, or use a wrapper like
# `env $(cat .env | xargs)` / direnv, or let the Laravel API pass them through).
# Copy to .env, fill in, never commit real values (.env is gitignored).

# Usage examples (run from engine/):
#   GEMINI_API_KEY=AIza... python3 coffee_clips.py "marte" --semantic --model gemini --classify
#   GEMINI_API_KEY=AIza... python3 coffee_clips.py "marte" --chat
#   COFFEE_SMTP_USER=me@gmail.com COFFEE_SMTP_PASS=app-password COFFEE_MAIL_TO=me@gmail.com \
#     python3 coffee_clips.py "agujero negro" --email
#   echo '{"action":"search","query":"marte"}' | python3 engine.py     # JSON contract
# Via the API you only set these in api/.env — Laravel passes them to the engine.

# --- AI (semantic search --model gemini, --classify, chat, book) ---
# Either variable works; GEMINI_API_KEY wins when both are set.
# Get a free key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey (looks like AIza...); leave empty to stay on local models.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
#GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# --- Email delivery (CLI --email; optional) ---
# Gmail needs an App Password (account with 2-step verification), not your login password.
# Commented out on purpose: setting any of these makes the engine treat SMTP as configured.
#COFFEE_SMTP_USER=me@gmail.com
#COFFEE_SMTP_PASS=abcd-efgh-ijkl-mnop
#COFFEE_MAIL_TO=me@gmail.com
#COFFEE_SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
#COFFEE_SMTP_PORT=587

# --- Path / feed overrides (optional; sensible defaults in coffee/config.py) ---
#COFFEE_FEED_URL=https://feeds.acast.com/public/shows/coffee-break-senal-y-ruido
#COFFEE_CACHE_DIR=cache
#COFFEE_OUTPUT_DIR=output
